    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d165">

                <pb facs="0297" n="235" sameAs="frus:frus1878/pg235"/>

                <head>No. 160.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Seward to Mr. von
                    Schlozer</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1878-05-01"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 1,
                        1878</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your note of the 8th ultimo,
                    in relation to the requirement by certain United States consuls in Germany of
                    samples of all goods exported to this country, I have now the honor to inclose a
                    copy of a letter of the 26th of April last upon the subject, which has been
                    received from the Secretary of the Treasury.</p>
                <p>It is proper to state that those consuls have been directed to comply strictly
                    with the instructions forbidding the exposure of samples to the observation of
                    competitors.</p>
                <p>Accept, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>F. W. SEWARD,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                        Secretary</hi>.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d165-a1.xml" xpointer="d165-a1"/>
            </div>
